WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.210
- As we celebrate the holidays,

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:04.210
we wanna shine a light on the millions

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:07.920
of moms out there making
Christmas happen all on their own.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.680
Kevin and I both were actually
raised by single mothers,

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.380
both of us know first-hand it ain't easy,

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.120
but somehow these super
women make miracles happen

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.630
for their families.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.830
That includes my next
guest, she's a single mom

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.980
from Kevin's hometown,
actually, of Philadelphia,

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.222
please welcome Andrea y'all.

00:00:24.222 --> 00:00:27.131
(applause)

00:00:27.131 --> 00:00:29.770
So tell us a little about yourself.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.700
- I'm just like Kevin, I
am from north Philadelphia.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.203
I'm a 25 year old single
mother of two amazing boys.

00:00:36.203 --> 00:00:40.500
My oldest son, his name is
Taylin, he's six years old.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.940
He's my little body guard.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.960
My youngest son's name is Mozzie,

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.810
he's autistic, special needs.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:48.610
He has a lotta sensory issues,

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:52.560
so he requires a lot
of attention and care.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.810
Right now, you know, all
three of us are sharing

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.170
a single room in my parent's home.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:01.570
It's very crowded, very hard
to study there, but you know.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:02.480
- Yeah, aren't you also,

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.860
you're studying to be a nurse, right?

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:05.570
- I am, I'm in school.

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:07.150
- How do you do that?

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.150
- I dunno, I just get
up every day and just,

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.120
you know, try to keep my
head up and remain positive

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.130
and do what I have to do.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:14.100
It's very hard.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.963
- So you've had a set back, what happened?

00:01:15.963 --> 00:01:19.470
- I found out that my
financial aid would not cover

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.193
my last year in nursing school.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:24.490
- And it's your last year?

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:27.520
- Yep, my last year, so, sorry.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.590
- That's okay, oh my gosh, wait.

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:32.610
See, I cry so often they
leave these by me, see?

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:35.830
- Thank you, so you know, right now,

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:36.760
you know I've been desperate,

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:40.881
I talked to the school, I tried
to apply for scholarships.

00:01:40.881 --> 00:01:42.410
I don't have the best of credit,

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:45.830
so I'm unable to apply for personal loans.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.430
So, you know, right now I have to drop out

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:51.250
of nursing school and I
only have one more year.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.240
You know I've been really
depressed about it,

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.090
a few days ago I had to
go in my closet and cry

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:58.300
because it makes me feel like
a failure as a mother because

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.690
- Oh my, okay, first of all, what?

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.360
You are not a failure as a mom,

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.730
I have cried in my bathroom with a bottle

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.530
and a glass of wine.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:07.650
You are not a failure.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:09.860
All of us go through
that, it doesn't matter,

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:10.890
dad's go through that.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:11.934
Every parent goes through that.

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:14.550
You want the best life for your kid,

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:17.360
and you try so hard, and some
days just don't work out.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:18.710
Well as I mentioned earlier,

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:21.185
both Kevin and I were
raised by single momma's.

00:02:21.185 --> 00:02:23.540
We know the holiday's can be tough.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.600
So Kevin, what's something
Andrea really needs

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:26.690
to understand?

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:29.420
- I think the best
thing to realize is that

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.920
you've done so well thus far.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:35.110
You know, you talk about two
boys that you're raising,

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.970
and that you're providing for,

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:41.200
and you're multitaskin'
from working to school.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.660
You've already done a lot.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:46.700
You've already checked
a lot of positive boxes,

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:50.320
and I think sometimes it's
important to really recognize

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:53.900
and realize what's
happened before we focus

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:56.180
on the thing that we feel hasn't happened.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:58.930
I'm not the most spiritual person,

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.520
but I believe that God, he
puts the toughest battles

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.270
on some of his strongest soldiers.

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:07.020
So, nothing that you can't handle is

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.780
not what you're going through,

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:10.840
like this is all a part of a plan.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:13.970
Who's plan, I don't know,
but it's supposed to happen

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:16.460
for a reason, and it's
only making you stronger.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.090
It's only making you better.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.930
And the better that you become,

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:22.990
the much better that those
boys'll become later on in life,

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:24.782
but you gotta check those positive boxes,

00:03:24.782 --> 00:03:26.510
and not the negative ones.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.283
That's the first piece of advice.

00:03:28.283 --> 00:03:29.700
- Man, well said.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:34.170
I need that advice in my life, Kevin.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:37.171
I'm on a couch right now, I'm at therapy.

00:03:37.171 --> 00:03:40.270
Single mom's pull off
miracles for their kids,

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:43.170
and I have no doubt Andrea
would pull off a miracle

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.980
for hers, but since it's
the season of miracles,

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:47.500
let's help her out.

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:52.500
Andrea, Kevin and I want to
Jumanji-size your Christmas.

00:03:52.878 --> 00:03:56.912
♪ Jumanji-size my Christmas ♪

00:03:56.912 --> 00:03:59.603
Yes.
- Jumanji-size.

00:03:59.603 --> 00:04:03.270
